  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure will continue to build across the\nMid-Atlantic and Carolinas tonight into Tuesday with a \ncooler/drier NE-E flow over the area bringing seasonable and \ncomfortable temps for early September, with highs in the low to \nmid 80s and dewpoints generally in the 60s. Temps will begin to\nwarm mid to late week as the high shifts offshore allowing \nsoutherly flow to re-develop ahead of the next front and high \ntemps climbing back into the upper 80s to lower 90s and dewpoint\ntemps into the low to mid 70s late in the week. Mostly dry \nweather will prevail through mid week as upper ridging build in\nfrom the west and a drier airmass in place, however a few shower\nwill linger across the offshore coastal waters through tonight. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...The upper ridge begins to break down for the\nlatter half of the week as a shortwave and attendant cold front\npush across the Midwest and Mid-Atlantic states. Guidance\ncontinues to show the front pushing into ENC on Friday and\nstalling along the coast through the weekend bringing unsettled\nweather across the region.",
